From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:39:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 40/43] vout: keep the eye correction of a 3D video with its
 file

Swap left and right eyes held for the video being played only, and the
next time the file opened its eyes were the wrong way round again.

Keep the correction with the file, as the stereo policy the programs of
the edition share does (the extended attribute
user.stereo-policy.swap-eyes, stereo_policy_set_file_swap_eyes()),
without rewriting the file: the menu shows what the file holds, and
clearing it removes the attribute. The input reads the file's correction
once, when it opens: the decoder applies it in the policy's decision,
over whatever packing was decided, and the video output shows only the
difference the user makes while it plays, so a correction is never
applied twice. A file that cannot keep it (read-only, remote, or on a
file system without extended attributes) keeps the correction for this
playback, and the user is told so.

First written by Daniel Ramos as patch 3d-0026 of the A10 field build
(vlc-stereo 3.0.24-1+stereo3d11~a10.1, 19 October 2026); the stereo
policy is optional here, as in the decoder.

Assisted-by: GPT-6 Astra via Codex
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
